# Lightstall Inquisitor and a modal double-faced card: Bot2 exiles Shatterskull Smashing and plays its back face, Shatterskull,
# the Hammer Pass, from exile as its land (CR 712.4, 305.1). Its own "you may pay 3 life. If you don't, it enters tapped"
# (CR 614.12) is paid, but the permission's "each land played this way enters tapped" (CR 614.1c) is a replacement of its
# own: the land still enters tapped, and Bot2 has paid the 3 life.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Lightstall Inquisitor
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Shatterskull Smashing
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightstall Inquisitor.Cast
Bot2.Choose(Shatterskull Smashing)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Exile.Shatterskull Smashing.Play
Bot2.Accept
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 2
Exile.Count = 0
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot2.Battlefield = Shatterskull, the Hammer Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Shatterskull, the Hammer Pass.Tapped = true
